{
  "version": 193,
  "released": "2026-08-22",
  "changelog": "v193: arc_walk — the arc-walking child interaction. Pressing Play on a SET of questions (a focus, a chapter, a book, the week's queue) now has a package behind it. NEW INTERACTION interactions/arc_walk/ (extends conversation 1.0.0, modes: walk), the fourth child of Conversation and the first whose Play approves nothing — the questions already exist, so only the conversation side runs. Its one goal: work a target's open questions casually, in resumable EPISODES. NEW MODULE system/arc_walk.py (pure; no writes, no model calls): build_arc_plan recomputes the target's open questions at every Play and NEVER persists them, ordering them by REUSING the weekly planner — question_planner.enriched_pending_questions for the weights, build_queue's own weight expression for the sort, and build_queue's arc_max streak cap as a deterministic re-order (both AST-pinned, so a planner change fails the build rather than letting a Play rank differently from the week) — with arc_planner card intents attached where cards exist. plan_n counts every question in the target and answered_k how many are answered, so 'k of N' is a bank fact and len(questions) == plan_n - answered_k by construction. Episode size by tier (basic 4 / standard 6 / extreme 8, capped at 12, well under knob.conversation_turn_cap_exchanges) ships as both module constants and knob.episode_size_* manifest knobs, pinned equal. arc_stage_for_session derives open|walk|close from the transcript plus the router's user_leaving signal; question_on_the_table names the qid a reply is answering. ONE ADDITIVE OUTPUT FIELD, answered_question_id (structural parse in conversation_delivery._parse_answered_question_id, closed validation in arc_walk.validate_answered_question_id against exact plan membership), gated on the new TurnShape.arc_stage — the fourth gate, and byte-identical output when it is None, which is the mechanical form of owner ruling 6: the passive daily single question is untouched. The 'asked qid' concept is NOT duplicated: it is the assistant turn's question_id (held_question_id to the model, stamped_question_id to the hosted platform) and arc_walk.asked_question_id is its one reader. Primary-only filing: an answer covering two questions names one. Seven arc_walk_gates.* lints (agenda announced once and never again, one question per reply, no counters, no mechanism talk, no pressure, a close that names what was covered and says the rest waits) scored over nine recorded goldens by the new arc-walk-evals harness. NEW READ-ONLY CLI arc-plan-target (--focus|--category|--chapter|--book|--queue [--episode-size N] [--json]) prints a plan and writes nothing. ADR 0023 records the episode/plan model, the not-persisted rule, primary-only filing, and 'passive users are untouched'; ADR 0018 gains the fourth-instance amendment row. Handbook: a new Arc Walk interaction page (behavior.md embedded byte-for-byte), the loop page's 'Play a focus = an episode of an arc plan, and it is the same ranking' note, and glossary entries for arc plan, episode, and arc walking — now real, not proposed. Contract: docs/pr-specs/arc-walk-interaction.md.",
